<section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="5f4f2259-2fef-4583-987d-86e9687e8b43"><problem><para>
      <para>How will the graph of k(x) = x be affected if the transformation k(x - 3) is applied?</para>
        </para></problem><solution><para>The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right.</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is: The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right. By applying the transformation \(k(x - 3)\), the graph is moved 3 units to the right, which shifts each point on the graph horizontally.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
